# /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env  (root:paperbot 640; made by an owner, never by install.sh). Optional.
# The real-money side writes through its OWN Telegram bot (a new bot made with @BotFather) to each owner's private
# chat with it, instead of the rule bot's room: the live paper bot (paperbot-combo), both executors
# (paperbot-executor, paperbot-executor-mexc) and the live checks (paperbot-livecheck, paperbot-livewatch) load this
# file AFTER live.env / executor.env, so the lines set here win. The rule bot and everything else keep live.env.
# Steps (docs/live1019-start-ko.md section 12, "실거래 텔레그램을 개인 채팅으로"):
#   1. @BotFather: /newbot, a name, a username ending in "bot"; keep the token on the server only;
#   2. each owner opens the new bot in Telegram, presses Start and sends it "hi";
#   3. sudo nano /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env with the token line below (no "#");
#   4. cd /opt/crypto-bot-research && sudo -u paperbot /opt/paperbot/venv/bin/python -m paperbot.livecheck chat-ids
#      (uses the token in effect: live.env, then this file; prints the private chats, never the token, sends nothing)
#   5. remove the "#" of the other lines and put both ids (comma-separated) on the three chat lines; restart.
# DANGER: a chat line left EMPTY (TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=) overrides live.env with nothing and the live bots fall back
# to the screen only. Keep a line commented out (#) rather than empty.
# 실거래 전용 봇 토큰(@BotFather에서 새로 만든 봇). 이 줄과 채팅 줄 3개는 함께 넣습니다(새 봇은 규칙봇 방에 없으므로 채팅 줄 없이 토큰만 넣으면 보내기가 실패합니다)
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=111,222
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO=
#TELEGRAM_SOUND=critical
#PAPERBOT_COMBO_TRADE_MSGS=0
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO: the same ids as CRITICAL (111,222). TELEGRAM_SOUND=critical rings only the
# alarms (🚨); "1" rings warnings too; unset or 0 keeps everything silent. PAPERBOT_COMBO_TRADE_MSGS=0: the live paper
# bot leaves its raw entry and exit lines out; the live watcher's 🟢 / 🔒 / ✅ / ❌ messages tell the trades instead.
# A token here with live.env's chats (the chat lines still commented out) reaches no one: after 10 minutes the live
# watcher says so once in the rule bot's room (through live.env's bot), and `livecheck show` prints it on its last line.
# executor.env may hold the same token and chats (the executors' alarms before this file existed): keeping both the
# same is fine; this file wins.
